   "content": "Maren found it at the base of the fog signal building, where the dune grass broke into gravel. A letter in a plastic grocery bag, the kind with blue handles. She picked it up by a corner and shook out three inches of sand.\n\nThe envelope had been through the wringer. Postmark from Harwich, Massachusetts. Dated June 3rd. It was now November. The ink had bled into something purple and illegible except for the recipient's name, which remained clear: *Dear Son.*\n\nShe carried it back along the concrete path. Her boots still rang with the day's chill. Inside the keeper's cottage, she set it on the kitchen table beside a cold cup of tea and a jar of WD-40 and a radio she hadn't turned on in two days because the frequency had gone dead.\n\nThe handwriting slanted left, the way schoolteachers corrected. The paper had softened to cloth along its edges, but the first line survived: *I should have said this differently.*\n\nShe sat. She read the whole thing. Then she folded it back along its original crease and put it in the drawer with the others.",
